### Querying the calendar -- ICalendarObjectContainer

It would be very resource intensive to request all events of a calendar only to then discard most of them during filtering. Instead, the client requests a certain set of objects (like the last 90 days) and the server will do the filtering. This can be achieved by the `SabreCalDAVICalendarObjectContainer` interface. Its sole method will return a list of entries. In contrast to the `getChildren()` method, the entries are not packed into their own objects. The client is responsible to do this by means of `getChild()` in a separate process. ```
<?php

function calendarQuery(array $filters) {
 // In a real implementation this should actually filter
 return ['test.ics'];
}
